  "frame_unit": "unit",
  "frame_description": "Traditional bird base with two lifted petal flaps. Adapted from examples/bird-base.cp: normalize to a unit square with y up, reorder vertices, add valley hinges 9-10 and 11-12, and leave the four outer midline segments flat. The inner axis points are 1 - 1/sqrt(2) from the centre. The old CP alone folds with all four corners together; these petal hinges lift SE and NW to the opposite tip. See examples/README.md for Oriedita's MIT provenance and the added construction. This endpoint does not specify the petal-fold motion.",
